{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00429",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.57,
      "end_seconds": 2.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Hello again. Come on in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.9,
      "end_seconds": 3.6,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hi."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 5.16,
      "end_seconds": 8.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.29,
      "end_seconds": 12.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Is this your first time with this clinic?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.85,
      "end_seconds": 17.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "So, mm, first time with this one, yes. A friend recommended it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.99,
      "end_seconds": 20.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "What's been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.54,
      "end_seconds": 28.84,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "I'm here because of headaches in the mornings. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.88,
      "end_seconds": 34.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "When did you first notice it? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.59,
      "end_seconds": 40.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "It's been two months, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.97,
      "end_seconds": 41.67,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.08,
      "end_seconds": 47.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Oh, and a little puffiness in the ankles. That's been about the same, two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.33,
      "end_seconds": 51.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.21,
      "end_seconds": 52.91,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.26,
      "end_seconds": 74.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Let me check a few things. Any breathlessness, vision changes or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.1,
      "end_seconds": 79.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "No breathlessness, vision changes or chest pain, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.33,
      "end_seconds": 82.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Are you on any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.81,
      "end_seconds": 86.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "No, uh, I don't take anything regularly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.44,
      "end_seconds": 93.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Okay, what about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.55,
      "end_seconds": 108.1,
      "duration_seconds": 14.55,
      "text": "Yes, I had a C-section, about ten years ago. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.99,
      "end_seconds": 112.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.55,
      "end_seconds": 120.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.63,
      "text": "Right, I've had high cholesterol for about a year now. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.59,
      "end_seconds": 122.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.97,
      "end_seconds": 126.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "No, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.8,
      "end_seconds": 130.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.61,
      "end_seconds": 146.81,
      "duration_seconds": 12.2,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.29,
      "end_seconds": 149.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.08,
      "end_seconds": 164.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.02,
      "end_seconds": 193.28,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 97 percent, temp 36.9 degrees, BP is 168 over 92, pulse is 91 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.54,
      "end_seconds": 197.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.89,
      "end_seconds": 201.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.11,
      "end_seconds": 215.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.68,
      "end_seconds": 218.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Stay still while I have a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.69,
      "end_seconds": 231.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "There's mild pitting swelling at both ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.65,
      "end_seconds": 257.03,
      "duration_seconds": 23.38,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. From what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with hypertension that isn't well controlled at this stage. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. I can't rule out a side effect from the current tablet yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.07,
      "end_seconds": 261.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Uh, is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.15,
      "end_seconds": 275.91,
      "duration_seconds": 13.76,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with hypertension that isn't well controlled do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had headaches in the mornings for two months, and no breathlessness or vision changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.22,
      "end_seconds": 279.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "So, um, exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.25,
      "end_seconds": 306.41,
      "duration_seconds": 25.16,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a lipid profile for cardiovascular risk. Let's use telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day, long term. You take it by mouth. That should help with high blood pressure. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Check the blood pressure at home, same time each morning, and write down the numbers for me. Salt is the big one, try to keep it low even though it's hard."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.36,
      "end_seconds": 325.41,
      "duration_seconds": 18.05,
      "text": "Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Let's review you in two weeks. Wonderful, I think that's it. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.43,
      "end_seconds": 330.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Okay, so that's everything I wanted to ask. Thank you."
    }
  ]
}